{{!-- A faction's name, and nothing else — the same reasoning as `route-header.hbs`.

      Core's page header carries a heading LEVEL and a "Display Page Title" switch, because a text
      page is a section of a document and those two decide how it folds into the table of
      contents. A faction is not a section of anything: it is one standing power in a region,
      drawn as its own block, and its title is always its name. --}}
<header class="journal-header">
    {{formInput fields.name value=name classes="title"
                aria=(object label=(localize "JOURNALENTRYPAGE.FIELDS.name.label"))
                placeholder=(localize "JOURNALENTRYPAGE.FIELDS.name.label")}}
</header>
